 2	
 3	Evidence behind [docs/01-landscape.md](../docs/01-landscape.md). Collected 2026-11-17.
 4	
 5	## adoption/
 6	
 7	| File | What it is | How to refresh |
 8	|---|---|---|
 9	| `adoption.json` | npm weekly and yearly downloads, registry metadata, jsDelivr monthly hits and GitHub stars for about fifty charting packages | `node fetch.mjs > adoption.json && node refill.mjs` |
10	| `httparchive.json` | Number of origins on which the HTTP Archive crawl detected each charting technology | `node httparchive.mjs > httparchive.json` |
11	| `cadence.json` | Major-version dates and stable release counts for the ten studied libraries | `node cadence.mjs` |
12	
13	The npm downloads API rate-limits bursts; `refill.mjs` retries the packages that came back empty.
14	
15	## harness/
16	
17	One page that runs the same tasks through ten libraries, and a probe that drives system Chrome through all of them.
18	
19	```bash
20	cd harness
21	npm install
22	npx vite build
23	npx vite preview --port 4173 --strictPort   # leave running
24	node probe.mjs            # all phases; or: node probe.mjs look | a11y | env | perf
25	node montage.mjs trend bars parts dirty empty kbd hover-la dark resize
26	node palette.mjs
27	node sizes.mjs
28	```
29	
30	| Path | Contents |
31	|---|---|
32	| `src/data.js` | The shared datasets. Every library receives exactly these values. |
33	| `src/libs/<library>.js(x)` | The least configuration each library needs for each task. Comments mark what was required beyond data. |
34	| `src/libs/<library>-tuned.js(x)` | The same large-data task using the fast path the library documents. |
35	| `probe.mjs` | DOM and accessibility-tree capture, keyboard walk, pointer hover in two time zones, resize, dark scheme, motion with and without reduced-motion, timings. |
36	| `results.json` | Probe output. |
37	| `shots/` | Screenshots; `_sheet-*.png` are the side-by-side sheets. |
38	| `palette.json`, `sizes.json` | Default palette scores and bundle sizes. |
39	
40	Open one case by hand at `http://localhost:4173/?lib=highcharts&task=trend`. Tasks: `trend`, `bars`, `parts`, `dirty`, `empty`, `scale&n=100000`, `stream`.
41	
42	## palette/
43	
44	`node search.mjs` searches for 6- and 8-color categorical palettes that reach 3:1 contrast on light and dark backgrounds while staying apart under simulated color-vision deficiencies. `feasibility.json` holds the result. It shows which thresholds are reachable; it is not Axylo's palette.
45	
46	## tables.mjs
47	
48	`node tables.mjs` prints the Markdown tables in the landscape report from the JSON files above.
49	
50	### Reading the timings
51	
52	Timings are from headless Chrome on one desktop machine, three runs each, and are meant for ranking by order of magnitude, not for precise comparison. "Time to second frame" is the time from calling the library to the second animation frame after it returns. It includes main-thread work and misses off-thread rasterization and any entry animation still running. Phase 3 replaces this with a stricter method ([docs/04-plan-performance.md](../docs/04-plan-performance.md)).
